WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.247
Voice Chief is in early access. Here is how
we set it up together.

2
00:00:05.047 --> 00:00:14.939
Voice Chief is in early access. Email
founder at ironvisiontools dot com to
request the app. Setup support is included,
so you do not set it up alone.

3
00:00:15.739 --> 00:00:24.795
We set up the bridge together on your own
server. Speech to text runs locally, so your
audio never leaves that machine. Your
terminal agent receives what you say.

4
00:00:25.595 --> 00:00:34.929
On your Windows PC you add the small
microphone app. We walk you through these
commands together: install the requirements,
copy the config file, then start the app.

5
00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:43.949
In the config file you enter your server
address. Together we check the address
works, so the microphone app can reach your
bridge before you try to talk.

6
00:00:44.749 --> 00:00:54.037
Next we bind a channel, which links your
terminal agent session to the voice app.
After that, what you say lands in that
session, and the answer comes back to you.

7
00:00:54.837 --> 00:01:05.379
Now hold the hotkey and speak. For example,
say: what is on my list today. Release the
key, and the agent answers out loud. You can
also type instead.

8
00:01:06.179 --> 00:01:11.334
Done. Need help? Email
support@ironvisiontools.com.
